  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py`, with tests in a new file, `tests/test_money.py`. The full suite passes: 13 tests, including the new ones.\n\n- **Behavior:** it returns `parts` integers that sum to `cents`. The remainder goes out one cent at a time starting from the first element, so `split(1000, 3)` gives `[334, 333, 333]`. If `parts` is below 1 it raises `ValueError`.\n- **Negative amounts:** I didn't handle these specially, and you didn't specify them. `split(-5, 3)` gives `[-1, -2, -2]`, which still sums to -5. The extra cent goes to the earlier elements, so those are the less negative ones.\n- **Tests:** they cover an even split, remainder placement, more parts than cents, a single part, zero, a negative amount, and invalid `parts` (0 and -1).\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
